  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_010 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc / 3.60 GPU hrs. Key findings: multiprofile >> single profile, transformer > avgpool aggregation, weighted > concat fusion, and imagenet_vit_l ≥ resnet50 (while being cheaper). The RNA encoder is the one major axis not yet varied within this best architecture. Question: Does scgpt (a generative-pretrained RNA encoder) produce better cell-level representations than scvi_n200 (a VAE) when paired with the strong ViT_L + transformer + weighted pipeline? This is a high-value exploration because if scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it confirms the architecture is robust to encoder choice; if it underperforms, it validates scvi_n200 as the right encoder and narrows the search. Cost: Expected training cost is comparable to config_010 (~3.5–4.5 GPU hrs) since the dominant cost drivers (ViT_L image processing, transformer aggregation) are identical; scgpt's forward pass is modestly more expensive than scvi_n200 but not dramatically so. With 4 experiments remaining, this is the best balance of exploitation (staying in the proven top architecture) and exploration (testing the last major untested variable), maximizing the chance of finding a >0.725 configuration before the budget ends."
}

